message: "If you use this software or build on its coordination stack, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "discrete-assembly-sim: An Open Coordination Stack for Discrete Lattice Assembly"
authors:
  - family-names: "Dyar"
    given-names: "Joshua"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-07-25
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/jdyar/discrete-assembly-sim"
abstract: >-
  A motion-invariant multi-robot coordination stack for discrete lattice
  assembly: validated build orders, cooperative choreography over a
  time-expanded graph with lease/deed reservations and placement gates,
  and in-situ error correction threaded through live reservations.
  Robot motion capability (reach, stride, climb, coupled pairs) and
  lattice geometry are injected as configuration. Includes an
  adversarial trap-fixture benchmark and a replayable run-log format.
